# The variables a target sets. Copy to .devopsy/.env for local work
# (gitignored); on servers each instance has its own shared/.env, written
# with `devopsy @<server>:<instance>/prod --vars set <NAME>` (the value
# from your environment or .env, else a prompt or stdin: never on the
# command line).

# The tunnel's token, from the Cloudflare dashboard (Networking, Tunnels:
# the tunnel's connector install command carries it). A secret
# (config.yaml's secrets: devopsy masks it). It only lets a connector run
# that tunnel: nothing else in the account. Required: a release fails
# before it goes live while it is unset.
#   devopsy @vm1:own/prod --vars set PROXY_TUNNEL_TOKEN
# A new one (refreshed in the dashboard) applies with
#   devopsy @vm1:own/prod --reload
#PROXY_TUNNEL_TOKEN=

# Where to release, instead of naming them in the address: the server
# (devopsy@203.0.113.10) and the instance (one per Cloudflare account).
#DEVOPSY_SERVER=
#DEVOPSY_INSTANCE=
